 "intro": {
  "title": "CHITIN AQUEDUCT",
  "lines": [
   "The only water on the world that still moves.",
   "It runs toward you, and it is the only way up."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Bellwright Yard, where the Bells are grown.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [70, 46],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Three channels stepped like a stair, and the water in every one of them runs toward me. The only water on this world I have seen move."
  },
  {
   "id": "current",
   "at": [64, 44],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Wading water pushes: with it you are fast, against it slow, and what wakes in it is carried down to you. The arc lamp conducts through it."
  },
  {
   "id": "hum",
   "at": [46, 44],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The channel hums when I put a hand in. Sound goes a long way down water. I think this is how the count reaches the cities."
  },
  {
   "id": "weir",
   "at": [14, 38],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A weir: the water falls down the ramp and you climb it. The banks on either side are dry; use them."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [30, 31],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: a rising note, a falling note, the same two, over and over. A question and an answer, I think. Nobody here is listening to either."
  },
  {
   "id": "east",
   "at": [66, 22],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The east weir is under a roof, and a shell-back stands in the water at its foot. The plate faces the current: take it from the bank."
  },
  {
   "id": "sluice-plate",
   "at": [24, 12],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "SLUICE PLATE",
   "text": "OPENED, AND CLOSED AGAIN BY HAND. THE WATER REMEMBERS THE COUNT. (The last line was added later, in a different hand, by someone who pressed hard.)"
  },
  {
   "id": "lever",
   "at": [18, 10],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The siphon: the whole aqueduct goes down this throat and comes out in the Deep. The lever on the north wall works the door to the exit."
  },
  {
   "id": "sluice",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The sluice shuts above the door. The door opens. The water goes on past it as if nothing had happened."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [60, 49],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The south wall of the bottom channel rings hollow here."
  }
 ],
